# =============================================================================
# Build-context exclusions.
#
# Both Dockerfiles use the repository ROOT as their build context (a pnpm
# workspace cannot be built from a subdirectory), so this file is doing real
# work: without it every `docker build` uploads node_modules, .next, the git
# pack and any local .env before the first instruction runs.
#
# Two rules that are not merely about speed:
#   * .env and infra/certs/ are excluded so a credential cannot be baked into
#     an image layer by an accidental `COPY . .` — layers are readable by
#     anyone who can pull the image (spec §73).
#   * node_modules is excluded because a host-installed tree contains binaries
#     built for the host's libc and CPU. Copying macOS/arm64 artefacts into a
#     linux/amd64 image produces failures that look like source bugs.
# =============================================================================

# ---- secrets and local state (never in an image) ----------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
infra/certs/
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
.npmrc
.netrc

# ---- version control --------------------------------------------------------
.git/
.gitignore
.gitattributes

# ---- dependencies (reinstalled inside the image for the target platform) ----
node_modules/
**/node_modules/
.pnpm-store/
**/.venv/
**/venv/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/.mypy_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
**/.pytest_cache/
**/*.egg-info/

# ---- build output (rebuilt inside the image) --------------------------------
**/.next/
**/out/
**/dist/
**/build/
**/.turbo/
**/coverage/
**/.tsbuildinfo
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# ---- editor / OS noise ------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ---- CI and infra: not needed by any application build ----------------------
# infra/ is excluded EXCEPT the Dockerfiles themselves, which BuildKit reads
# via -f before the context is sent, so their exclusion here is harmless.
.github/
infra/docker-compose.yml
infra/scripts/
infra/seed/

# ---- docs: large, and nothing in an image reads them ------------------------
# The 5,400-line spec plus the architecture docs are pure context weight.
docs/
*.md
!apps/api/README.md
!apps/web/README.md
# apps/api/README.md is kept because pyproject.toml declares it as the project
# readme and hatchling reads it during `pip install .`.

# ---- test artefacts ---------------------------------------------------------
**/tests/__snapshots__/
**/playwright-report/
**/test-results/

# ---- logs -------------------------------------------------------------------
*.log
npm-debug.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
